messages.content:
{
  "message": "Yes—please proceed to power off and reseat the physical SIM now. After it boots back up, turn Mobile Data ON so the phone can register on the network. Here’s exactly what to do on your Samsung Galaxy S21.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "Airplane Mode is now OFF, but the phone still isn’t registered. A SIM reseat fixes most “No SIM/No Signal” issues caused by poor contact.",
    "“Data Disabled” prevents network registration for data; turning it ON helps the device complete registration and show bars/4G/5G."
  ],
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "step": "Power OFF and reseat the SIM",
      "how": "Turn the phone completely OFF. Use the SIM eject tool on the top edge SIM tray. Remove the tray, place the SIM flat with gold contacts facing down and the notched corner aligned, then reinsert the tray fully and firmly."
    },
    {
      "step": "Power ON and wait",
      "how": "Turn the phone back ON and wait up to 2 minutes for network registration.",
      "check": "See if the status bar changes from “No Signal” to show bars or a network type (4G/LTE/5G)."
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn Mobile Data ON",
      "how": "Swipe down twice to open Quick Panel > tap Mobile Data to turn it ON (or go to Settings > Connections > Data usage > Mobile data ON).",
      "check": "Confirm the “Data Disabled” notice goes away."
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm Airplane Mode stays OFF",
      "how": "In Quick Panel, ensure the airplane icon is NOT highlighted."
    }
  ],
  "please_reply_with": [
    "After the SIM reseat and reboot: do you see any bars or network type (4G/LTE/5G), or still “No SIM/No Signal”?",
    "Any on-screen prompts like “Enter SIM PIN,” “SIM not provisioned,” or “Emergency calls only”?",
    "Confirmation that Mobile Data is ON and the “Data Disabled” notice is gone."
  ],
  "what_i_will_do_next": "While you perform the SIM reseat and reboot, I will check the specific line on your account that corresponds to 555-123-2002 (from your list of lines) to verify its status (Active vs. Suspended), contract dates, and roaming configuration. I will share the findings as soon as you report back."
}

