messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the details. Seeing “No signal” plus “Data disabled” means your phone isn’t connected to the cellular network right now. MMS won’t work until we restore cellular service and mobile data. Turning off Wi‑Fi Calling at this moment won’t help (and could reduce your ability to call while there’s no cellular signal), so let’s keep it ON for now. We’ll only toggle Wi‑Fi Calling OFF later when we test MMS after signal is back.",
  "request_for_identification": "To check your line status on our side (e.g., suspension, roaming, data plan), please share ONE of the following: 1) the phone number of the affected line, or 2) your customer ID, or 3) your full name and date of birth (YYYY‑MM‑DD).",
  "questions": [
    "Are you using a physical SIM or an eSIM?",
    "Are you currently traveling outside your home network area (roaming)?",
    "Did this start after any recent change (SIM swap, device update, moving to a new area)?"
  ],
  "plan_of_action_explained": "We’ll do two tracks in parallel. 1) Account-side: I’ll verify if the line is active, not suspended, and whether roaming is enabled (needs your account ID/number). 2) Device-side: We’ll restore cellular service by ruling out Airplane Mode, SIM issues, and network settings. Once bars return, we’ll confirm mobile data and then test MMS (and briefly toggle Wi‑Fi Calling if needed).",
  "device_steps_now": [
    {
      "step": "Check Airplane Mode",
      "how": "Open quick settings and make sure Airplane Mode is OFF. If it was ON, turn it OFF and wait 30–60 seconds to see if signal bars return.",
      "why": "Airplane Mode disables all radios, causing no signal and data disabled."
    },
    {
      "step": "Refresh the radio",
      "how": "Toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then OFF. Wait up to 60 seconds for bars to appear.",
      "why": "Forces the phone to re-register with the network."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check SIM status",
      "how": "In Settings (or using the diagnostic action), run check_sim_status. If it shows ‘Missing’, reseat the SIM (remove and reinsert) using reseat_sim_card. If it shows ‘Locked’, don’t guess the PIN/PUK—tell me what it shows. If ‘Active’, proceed.",
      "why": "A missing or locked SIM prevents any cellular connection."
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify network mode",
      "how": "Run check_network_mode_preference. If it’s set to 2G/3G only, change it to set_network_mode_preference = \"4g_5g_preferred\".",
      "why": "Older modes can block modern network attachment and data."
    },
    {
      "step": "Toggle mobile data",
      "how": "Once you have at least some signal bars, ensure mobile data is ON (toggle_data OFF then ON).",
      "why": "The status bar can show ‘data disabled’ when there’s no signal; we’ll re-enable it after signal returns."
    },
    {
      "step": "APN quick check (only if data still fails with signal present)",
      "how": "Run check_apn_settings. If MMSC is missing/incorrect, run reset_apn_settings, then reboot_device.",
      "why": "Incorrect APN/MMSC blocks MMS even when data works."
    },
    {
      "step": "MMS test",
      "how": "After you have signal and mobile data is ON, briefly turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling and Wi‑Fi, then send a small photo MMS to your own number as a test. Turn Wi‑Fi Calling back ON afterward.",
      "why": "Some networks don’t carry MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling; testing over cellular confirms MMS is fixed."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "Your account identifier (phone number/customer ID/name+DOB) so I can check the line on our side.",
    "Results of each step above: Airplane Mode status, SIM status (Active/Missing/Locked), current network mode, whether any signal bars appear, and whether mobile data shows as enabled after bars return.",
    "If you are traveling/roaming right now."
  ],
  "notes": "If after steps 1–4 you still see ‘No signal’, I’ll immediately check your line’s status for suspension or roaming configuration and fix what’s eligible on our side once you provide your account details."
}

