messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the detailed updates. Since your line is active, data is ON, Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF, Data Saver is OFF, and APN was reset + rebooted, the next most likely blockers are the messaging app’s permissions/background data, a VPN interfering, or (less likely) an APN/MMSC entry not taking effect. None of the steps below will affect your photos or personal files. Please follow these in order and report back what you find.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Allow the Messages app required permissions",
      "why": "MMS needs access to SMS and storage/photos to attach and send media.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (your default SMS app).",
        "Permissions > ensure SMS is Allowed.",
        "Also allow Photos and videos (or Storage).",
        "Return to the app and try sending an MMS again (Wi‑Fi OFF, mobile data ON)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable background/Unrestricted data for Messages",
      "why": "If background data is restricted, MMS may fail to send.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages > Mobile data & Wi‑Fi (or Data usage).",
        "Turn ON Background data.",
        "If you see ‘Unrestricted data’ or ‘Allow data usage while Data Saver is on’, turn it ON as well.",
        "Retry sending an MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check and, if needed, disconnect any VPN",
      "why": "Some VPNs interfere with MMS routing.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN.",
        "If a VPN is Connected, tap it and Disconnect.",
        "Retry sending an MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify the APN’s MMSC field is populated",
      "why": "MMS requires a valid MMSC URL. We reset APN already, but let’s confirm it stuck.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the active APN (the one with the radio dot selected).",
        "Scroll to MMSC and confirm it has a URL filled in (not blank).",
        "If it’s blank, use Menu (⋮) > Reset to default again, then restart the phone and retry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional sanity check: Preferred network mode",
      "why": "You’re seeing 5G already, but let’s confirm it’s not set to a legacy mode.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Preferred network type.",
        "Select 4G/5G preferred."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next_action_request": "Please try the steps above in order. Then tell me: 1) Which ‘Messages’ app you have (Google Messages or Samsung Messages), 2) whether SMS and Photos/Storage permissions were allowed, 3) whether Background data/Unrestricted data were ON, 4) whether a VPN was connected, and 5) whether the MMSC field was populated. Also share any exact error message shown when sending the MMS. Based on your results, I’ll guide you through the final steps. If it still fails after these checks, we can reseat the SIM and perform one more targeted test before escalating."
}

