messages.content:
{
  "reasoning": "MMS needs two key permissions in your texting app: SMS (to send/receive messages) and Photos/Storage (to attach media). Since only Phone is granted, the app can’t send picture messages. Granting these does not affect or delete your photos.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Open your texting app’s App info",
      "options": [
        "Settings > Apps > See all apps (or App list) > find and tap your messaging app.",
        "OR: Find the texting app icon on your home screen/app drawer, press and hold it, then tap the small “i” (App info)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grant SMS permission",
      "how": [
        "In App info, tap Permissions.",
        "Tap SMS (or Text messages) and choose Allow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grant Photos/Storage permission",
      "how": [
        "Still in Permissions, look for Photos and videos (Android 13+) or Storage/Files and media (older versions).",
        "Tap it and choose Allow."
      ],
      "note": "If you see both ‘Photos and videos’ and ‘Music and audio’, allow Photos and videos. Storage/Files and media is the older equivalent—allow it if that’s what your phone shows."
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional: Confirm it’s the Default SMS app",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Apps > Default apps > SMS app.",
        "Ensure your messaging app is selected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS",
      "how": [
        "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF, keep Mobile data ON, and make sure Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF (as you already did).",
        "Open the messaging app, start a new message, attach a small photo, and send.",
        "Observe any error message, if shown."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next_action_request": "Please grant SMS and Photos/Storage (or Photos and videos) permissions as above, then try sending an MMS again. Tell me: 1) the exact app name you see in App info, 2) which permissions you enabled, and 3) what happens when you try to send the MMS (including any error message). If it still fails, I’ll guide you through the next targeted checks."
}

