      "usage_this_cycle_gb": 8.7,
      "roaming_enabled_on_line": true,
      "notes": "No suspension or data-cap block detected."
    }
  },
  "thought_process": "Your line is active, under the data limit, and roaming is enabled on our side. Since you’re in France and can’t browse on mobile data, the most likely causes are device-level settings: data roaming OFF on the phone, mobile data OFF, unsuitable network mode (e.g., stuck on 2G), VPN/Data Saver interference, Wi‑Fi Calling interaction, or APN/MMSC configuration. We’ll check and fix these step by step.",
  "steps_for_you": [
    {
      "step": "1. Check core connection on the phone",
      "why": "Confirms whether mobile data and roaming are enabled on the device and what network you’re on.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_network_status and share what it shows (airplane mode, signal strength, network type like 4G/5G/2G, Mobile Data ON/OFF, Data Roaming ON/OFF).",
        "If Mobile Data is OFF, use toggle_data to turn it ON.",
        "If Data Roaming is OFF, use toggle_roaming to turn it ON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "2. Prefer modern networks",
      "why": "MMS needs at least 3G; 4G/5G is best. Older modes can block data.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_network_mode_preference.",
        "If you see 2G/3G only, use set_network_mode_preference with mode \"4g_5g_preferred\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "3. Eliminate common blockers",
      "why": "VPN, Data Saver, and Wi‑Fi Calling can interfere with data/MMS while roaming.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_vpn_status. If connected, use disconnect_vpn.",
        "Run check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON, use toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Run check_wifi_calling_status. If Wi‑Fi Calling is ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF temporarily."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "4. Verify APN and MMSC",
      "why": "Incorrect APN/MMSC commonly breaks MMS, especially when roaming.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_apn_settings and tell me the APN name and whether an MMSC URL is set.",
        "If APN looks incorrect or MMSC is missing, use reset_apn_settings, then use reboot_device to restart the phone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "5. Quick data test and MMS test",
      "why": "Confirms that mobile data works before retrying MMS.",
      "actions": [
        "After steps above (and reboot if you reset APN), make sure Wi‑Fi is OFF.",
        "Run run_speed_test and share the result.",
        "Try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "6. If MMS still fails, check app permissions",
      "why": "The messaging app needs storage and SMS permissions for MMS.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_app_permissions for your messaging app (e.g., \"Messages\").",
        "If storage or sms permissions aren’t granted, use grant_app_permission for \"storage\" and \"sms\"."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_reply_with": [
    "Results of check_network_status (especially Mobile Data and Data Roaming, and the network type).",
    "Your current network mode preference.",
    "Whether VPN, Data Saver, or Wi‑Fi Calling were ON and what you changed.",
