  "acknowledgement": "You’re right — those statuses will prevent MMS from sending. Let’s fix them step by step.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs an active SIM, cellular signal, mobile data ON, and (if you’re outside your home network) data roaming ON. Airplane Mode disables radios; a missing SIM prevents any network registration; data/roaming OFF blocks MMS.",
  "steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Turn OFF Airplane Mode",
      "how": "Open Quick Settings and tap the airplane icon to turn it OFF, or go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Airplane mode and switch it OFF.",
      "why": "Re‑enables cellular and other radios."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check SIM status; reseat if still missing",
      "how": "If it still says SIM missing: power the phone OFF. Eject the SIM tray, remove the SIM, gently wipe the gold contacts with a lint‑free cloth, ensure correct orientation, reinsert fully, then power ON.",
      "why": "Ensures proper contact with the SIM reader so the phone can register on the network.",
      "safety_note": "Always power OFF before removing/inserting the SIM."
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn ON Mobile Data",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network (or SIMs) > turn Mobile data ON.",
      "why": "MMS uses mobile data."
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn ON Data Roaming (if you’re outside your home network)",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Roaming ON. Accept any prompts.",
      "why": "Allows data over partner networks when traveling."
    },
    {
      "step": "Set Preferred Network to 4G/5G",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Preferred network type > select 4G/5G.",
      "why": "Ensures adequate connectivity for MMS."
    },
    {
      "step": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for the test",
      "how": "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF temporarily in Quick Settings.",
      "why": "Forces MMS to use mobile data (some setups don’t send MMS over Wi‑Fi)."
    },
    {
      "step": "Send a small photo MMS",
      "how": "Send to yourself first, then to one known contact. Wait up to 1–2 minutes for status to change to Sent.",
      "why": "Confirms MMS end‑to‑end."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_expect": [
    "After Airplane Mode is OFF and the SIM is detected, you should see signal bars and a network indicator like 4G/LTE/5G.",
    "With Mobile Data and (if applicable) Data Roaming ON, the MMS should move from “Sending” to “Sent” within 1–2 minutes."
  ],
  "if_issue_persists": [
    "If SIM still shows Missing after reseating: in Settings > Network & Internet > SIMs, ensure the SIM toggle is ON. If possible, test your SIM in another phone or try a known‑good SIM in your phone to isolate SIM vs. device.",
    "If SIM is detected but MMS still hangs: ensure Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF, Data Saver is OFF, no VPN is active; then reset APN to default (Settings > Mobile network > Access Point Names > Reset to default) and reboot before retrying.",
    "Try sending a smaller photo."
  ],
  "offer_help": "If the SIM remains undetected in multiple devices or you see SIM lock (PIN/PUK) prompts you can’t resolve, tell me and I can arrange a transfer to a human agent for SIM replacement or further diagnostics.",
  "ask_for_update": "Please follow the steps and let me know: does the SIM show as detected, do you see signal bars/4G or 5G, and does the test MMS send? Based on what you observe, I’ll guide you further."
}

